      "name": "STATUS",
      "kind": "ro",
      "desc": "Host state",
      "fields": [
        {
          "port": "cmd_busy",
          "desc": "a command is running (sending, or waiting for the BTA response)"
        },
        {
          "port": "tx_oe",
          "desc": "the host owns the lane (low during the bus turn-around)"
        },
        {
          "port": "pkt_cnt",
          "desc": "packets sent (wraps)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "BTA",
      "kind": "ro",
      "desc": "Read response",
      "fields": [
        {
          "port": "bta_data",
          "desc": "{data1, data0, DI} of the last accepted response, single-bit errors corrected"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "irqs": [
    {
      "name": "BTA_DONE",
      "port": "bta_done",
      "desc": "a read response was accepted (BTA holds it)"
    },
    {
      "name": "ERROR",
      "port": "irq",
      "desc": "a command rejected, an Acknowledge-and-Error-Report response with error bits, no response within BTA_TO (512) clocks, a bad SoT byte or an uncorrectable response header"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "tx_bit and tx_valid (the HS lane, one bit per PCLK, LSB first, idle 1), tx_oe (the host owns the lane) and rx_bit (driven by the peripheral after the turn-around) pass through unchanged; tx_oe is also readable in STATUS.",
    "PL0..PL31 write the 32-byte payload RAM (write only, whole words: a partial-strobe write gets PSLVERR). The lane states (LP, HS entry) are abstracted to tx_valid."
  ]
